# Test: a held live refresh shows the paused mark, and Apply now applies it
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-ui-1 user story 4 with the closure review's held
#            refresh finding -- while a region holds its refresh for what the
#            operator is doing in the browser, the page says so near the live
#            banner, and its Apply now control fetches the waiting refresh
# PREVENTS: a page that holds its refresh with no sign of it, looking live
#           while it shows what was read before the event, for as long as a
#           row stays ticked
#
# Question: does the page show that it holds a refresh, and does the
# operator's Apply now land it? Only a browser decides it: the hold, the
# mark and the control are fleet.js state over a live event stream.
# Method: the review build starts with its sample script held, so the estate
# changes only when the header's Step is pressed. core-par-02 is offline from
# the start (sample/estate.go offlineFor), so the devices table filtered to
# state:offline holds its row; the script's first step takes cpe-lon-03
# offline, which adds it to that table. The test ticks core-par-02 and steps:
# the root carries data-fleet-held, the paused mark is shown and the table
# still lacks cpe-lon-03. Apply now, with the row still ticked, lands the
# refresh: the table shows cpe-lon-03 and the mark is gone. Every wait is on
# state the page shows, never on a time.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_fleet_ui_sample:state=present
option=env:var=ze.web.fleet.sample.held:value=true
option=timeout:value=90s
option=viewport:width=1600:height=1000

action=open:path=/fleet/estate/devices/?q=state%3Aoffline
expect=html:id=fleet-content:contains=core-par-02
expect=html:id=fleet-content:not-contains=cpe-lon-03
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-fleet-stream:value=open
expect=element:not-text=Live updates are paused

action=click:text=Select core-par-02
expect=attribute:selector=tr.fleet-table-row--selected:name=class:contains=fleet-table-row--selected

# Step 1: cpe-lon-03 goes offline, and the content is stale. Its refresh
# waits, and the page says so.
action=click:id=fleet-proto-step
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-fleet-held:value=true
expect=element:text=Live updates are paused
expect=html:id=fleet-content:not-contains=cpe-lon-03

# Apply now lands the refresh although the row is still ticked.
action=click:text=button "Apply now"
expect=html:id=fleet-content:contains=cpe-lon-03
expect=element:not-text=Live updates are paused
